From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: request optional firmware-2.bin directly

ath11k treats firmware-2.bin as optional and falls back to API 1 when
the file is not present. Request it with request_firmware_direct(),
which checks the filesystem without invoking the userspace firmware
helper. This avoids unnecessary firmware hotplug requests and procd
warnings for a file that is not required by the API 1 fallback path.

Keep the existing error handling so a missing API 2 container continues
to select the existing API 1 firmware loading path.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/fw.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/fw.c
@@ -16,10 +16,14 @@ static int ath11k_fw_request_firmware_api_n(struct ath11k_base *ab,
 	struct ath11k_fw_ie *hdr;
 	const u8 *data;
 	__le32 *timestamp;
-
-	ab->fw.fw = ath11k_core_firmware_request(ab, name);
-	if (IS_ERR(ab->fw.fw)) {
-		ret = PTR_ERR(ab->fw.fw);
+	char path[100];
+
+	/* The file is optional: look for it on the filesystem only, so a
+	 * missing one does not go through the user-space fallback loader.
+	 */
+	ath11k_core_create_firmware_path(ab, name, path, sizeof(path));
+	ret = request_firmware_direct(&ab->fw.fw, path, ab->dev);
+	if (ret) {
 		ath11k_dbg(ab, ATH11K_DBG_BOOT, "failed to load %s: %d\n", name, ret);
 		ab->fw.fw = NULL;
 		return ret;
--
2.53.0
